preConditionHook:
// THE FIRST PULLBACK ARRIVES LATE. This bar is the first bar since the
// breakout whose low is below the prior bar's low, and it is at least
// minBarsBeforePullback bars after that breakout. Brooks's leading sign of
// breakout strength -- 'the first pullback occurs only after three or more
// bars of breaking out'. NEGATED with the per-placement toggle it is his sign
// of weakness ('the first pullback occurs two bars after the reversal'), and
// at minBarsBeforePullback = 6 it is the other bound he states ('any pullback
// should come within five bars or so').
//
// THE BREAKOUT ANCHOR is a close above EL's Highest(high, breakoutLookback)[1]
// -- the N bars ENDING ONE BAR AGO -- the same fresh-N-bar-extreme anchor the
// rest of this bucket uses. Extremes() is EasyLanguage source, so the scan
// carries the relational tolerance through el_gt / el_lt.
//
// 'NO EARLIER PULLBACK BAR SINCE THE BREAKOUT' is carried as a RUNNING
// MINIMUM, not as Lowest(low, barsSince)[1]: the bars-since count is
// unbounded before the first breakout of a run, and a window of that length
// would index past Max Bars Back. prevMinLow holds the lowest low from the
// breakout bar through the PREVIOUS bar, which is exactly what
// Lowest(low, barsSince)[1] would return, and nothing here reaches deeper
// than breakoutLookback. On the breakout bar itself that window is empty and
// prevMinLow is seeded with the previous bar's low, so the test degenerates
// to true -- which only matters at minBarsBeforePullback = 0.
//
// Warm-up: before the first breakout the running minimum is still its initial
// 0 and the test cannot pass on positive prices; the EasyLanguage twin's
// variable initialises to the same 0.
//
// Not PullbackDurationBars, which reads the same anchor's bars-since as an
// upper bound and adds no pullback-bar test.
priorHigh = high[1];
priorLow = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)breakoutLookback; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], priorHigh)) priorHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], priorLow)) priorLow = low[i];
}
if (el_gt(close[0], priorHigh)) {
    barsSinceBoUp = 0;
    prevMinLow = low[1];
    minLowSinceBo = low[0];
} else {
    barsSinceBoUp = barsSinceBoUp + 1;
    prevMinLow = minLowSinceBo;
    if (el_lt(low[0], minLowSinceBo)) minLowSinceBo = low[0];
}
if (el_lt(close[0], priorLow)) {
    barsSinceBoDn = 0;
    prevMaxHigh = high[1];
    maxHighSinceBo = high[0];
} else {
    barsSinceBoDn = barsSinceBoDn + 1;
    prevMaxHigh = maxHighSinceBo;
    if (el_gt(high[0], maxHighSinceBo)) maxHighSinceBo = high[0];
}
